Here's something the SE Linux crowd might want to keep an eye on in case
the standard takes off with the idea being making sure SE Linux meets the
standard.=20

"This standard will enable mass production of a class of operating systems
that meet the minimum expectations of consumers for security and general
reliability by establishing a floor for these characteristics," says Jack
Cole, IEEE P2200 Working Group Chair.

Minimum security standards for consumer OS's sure would be nice!

